            question: 'Explain Information Provision as a government solution to market failure.',
            answer: 'Government can correct information failure by providing accurate information to help consumers make better decisions:\n\n1. Public Awareness Campaigns: Government educates the public about risks of demerit goods and benefits of merit goods through advertising and media campaigns.\n\n2. Mandatory Labeling: Requiring products to display information such as nutritional content, health warnings, or environmental impact helps consumers make informed choices.\n\n3. Correcting Information Asymmetry: Government provides unbiased information to reduce information gap between producers and consumers.\n\n4. Singapore Examples:\n- Health Promotion Board campaigns on healthy eating and exercise\n- Graphic warnings on cigarette packets about health risks\n- Nutritional labels on food products (Healthier Choice Symbol)\n- Energy efficiency labels on appliances\n- Ministry of Education campaigns on importance of education\n- Public safety announcements and advisories\n\n5. Impact: Better information helps consumers understand true costs and benefits, leading to more optimal consumption decisions and reducing overconsumption of demerit goods and underconsumption of merit goods.\n\n6. Cost-Effective: Information provision is relatively cheap compared to other interventions.',
