            question: 'What are the roles of Private and Public Sectors in a Mixed Economy?',
            answer: 'In a mixed economy, both sectors play distinct roles:\n\nPrivate Sector:\n- Produces most consumer goods and services\n- Driven by profit motive and competition\n- Makes decisions based on price signals\n- Provides employment and innovation\n- Responds quickly to consumer demands\n- Examples: Retail shops, private companies, restaurants\n\nPublic Sector:\n- Provides public goods (defence, street lighting)\n- Supplies merit goods at subsidized rates (healthcare, education, public housing)\n- Regulates private sector activities\n- Redistributes income through taxes and transfers\n- Stabilizes the economy through fiscal policy\n- Examples in Singapore: HDB, public hospitals, MRT (government-linked), schools\n\nThe balance between sectors determines the degree of government intervention. Singapore has significant government involvement in housing, healthcare, education, and transport while maintaining a strong private sector in most other areas.',
